1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:01,490
Six hundred and twenty per cent.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:05,690
That's how much sales of one Chinese
electric SUV jumped in Australia in a

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:09,370
single month of 2026,
compared with the year before.

4
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:13,010
A car most Australians had never heard
of two years ago is now inside the

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:14,110
national top ten.

6
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,450
And it's not alone.

7
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,450
One electric SUV more than doubled
its sales and finished most months as

8
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,390
Australia's best-selling EV.

9
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:24,704
One brand you've probably never driven
grew more than one thousand five

10
00:00:24,754 --> 00:00:25,450
hundred per cent.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,670
A small Chinese SUV is
outselling the Hyundai Kona.

12
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,770
And Toyota's most famous ute
just roared back to number one.

13
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:37,550
2026 has been the most dramatic year
for new cars in Australia in decades.

14
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,490
October was the biggest October ever,

15
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,530
and the market passed one
million sales before November.

16
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:45,230
But the winners aren't the cars
you'd have guessed five years ago.

17
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,230
So in this video,

18
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:50,470
I'm counting down the ten cars
Australians went crazy for in 2026.

19
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:52,490
Real sales numbers, real growth,

20
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:55,850
and the reason each one is winning
including the one at number one,

21
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,470
which changed the Australian
car market forever.

22
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,470
And stay to the end,

23
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,660
because I'll tell you what these winners
mean for the price of your next car.

24
00:01:03,201 --> 00:01:04,991
First, a quick look at the scoreboard,

25
00:01:05,041 --> 00:01:07,951
because it explains why this
list looks the way it does.

26
00:01:08,001 --> 00:01:13,791
Australians bought 107,493
new vehicles in October 2026,

27
00:01:13,841 --> 00:01:15,151
a record for the month.

28
00:01:15,201 --> 00:01:18,551
Year to date, the market has
already passed one million sales.

29
00:01:18,601 --> 00:01:19,911
But where did the money go?

30
00:01:19,961 --> 00:01:24,951
Electric car sales in October were
up 237 per cent on October last year,

31
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:28,331
and electric cars took more
than 23 per cent of the market.

32
00:01:28,381 --> 00:01:32,811
BYD sold more than ten thousand cars
in a single month and is now firmly the

33
00:01:32,861 --> 00:01:36,311
second biggest brand in
Australia, behind only Toyota.

34
00:01:36,361 --> 00:01:38,851
Cars built in China were up 104 per cent.

35
00:01:38,901 --> 00:01:43,367
In the first nine months of the
year, Geely was up 639 per cent.

36
00:01:43,417 --> 00:01:46,671
Omoda Jaecoo was up 621 per cent.

37
00:01:46,721 --> 00:01:50,671
And Zeekr was up a
staggering 1,560 per cent.

38
00:01:50,721 --> 00:01:54,591
Meanwhile, plenty of familiar
names went backwards Mitsubishi,

39
00:01:54,641 --> 00:02:00,071
Subaru, Nissan, Volkswagen, Hyundai
and Mazda all had double-digit falls.

40
00:02:00,121 --> 00:02:02,311
So what makes a winner in 2026?

41
00:02:02,361 --> 00:02:04,711
Price, technology, and timing.

42
00:02:04,761 --> 00:02:06,991
The winners on this
list are mostly cheaper,

43
00:02:07,041 --> 00:02:10,031
newer, and more efficient than the
cars they're replacing in buyers'

44
00:02:10,081 --> 00:02:10,671
driveways.

45
00:02:10,721 --> 00:02:14,091
But not all of them are Chinese and
two of the biggest comebacks are from

46
00:02:14,141 --> 00:02:14,971
Toyota.

47
00:02:15,021 --> 00:02:16,611
A quick note on the numbers.

48
00:02:16,661 --> 00:02:21,451
I'm using official VFACTS figures
through CarExpert, CarsGuide and GoAuto.

49
00:02:21,501 --> 00:02:23,131
Tesla doesn't report to VFACTS,

50
00:02:23,181 --> 00:02:25,711
so its figures come from the
Electric Vehicle Council.

51
00:02:25,761 --> 00:02:26,561
Let's go.

52
00:02:28,173 --> 00:02:30,018
Number ten: the BYD Atto 2.

53
00:02:30,068 --> 00:02:35,525
The Atto 2 is a small SUV, and it's one
of BYD's newest models in Australia.

54
00:02:35,575 --> 00:02:37,425
And it took off almost straight away.

55
00:02:37,475 --> 00:02:39,485
In the first half of 2026,

56
00:02:39,535 --> 00:02:42,215
the Atto 2 sold 5,401 cars,

57
00:02:42,265 --> 00:02:47,185
according to CarExpert putting it in a
close race for BYD's third-best seller.

58
00:02:47,235 --> 00:02:48,085
And in October,

59
00:02:48,135 --> 00:02:50,725
it was the eighth best-selling
vehicle in the entire country,

60
00:02:50,775 --> 00:02:53,685
with 1,943 sales.

61
00:02:53,735 --> 00:02:56,385
A brand-new nameplate,
inside the national top ten.

62
00:02:56,435 --> 00:02:58,365
Part of the reason is price.

63
00:02:58,415 --> 00:03:05,245
BYD now offers a plug-in hybrid
Atto 2 DM-i at $25,990 drive-away.

64
00:03:05,295 --> 00:03:09,545
That's cheaper than many petrol small
SUVs, with much lower fuel bills.

65
00:03:09,595 --> 00:03:12,065
The Atto 2 shows how BYD wins:

66
00:03:12,115 --> 00:03:16,225
not with one hero car, but with a whole
wall of models at every price point.

67
00:03:16,275 --> 00:03:17,985
If buyers don't want the Atto 2,

68
00:03:18,035 --> 00:03:21,785
there's the Atto 1 for $19,990 drive-away,

69
00:03:21,835 --> 00:03:24,805
or the Sealion 5, 6, 7 or 8.

70
00:03:24,855 --> 00:03:28,575
And that's exactly why BYD has become
the number two brand in Australia.

71
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:32,520
Number nine: the GWM Haval Jolion.

72
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:35,420
While other brands struggled,
the Jolion just kept growing.

73
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:37,700
In the first nine months of 2026,

74
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:41,300
it sold 17,051 cars, up 20 per cent,

75
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:44,560
and it finished ninth in the
national year-to-date rankings.

76
00:03:44,610 --> 00:03:46,860
That puts it above some very big names.

77
00:03:46,910 --> 00:03:48,880
It's ahead of the Mazda CX-5,

78
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:53,280
the Kia Sportage and the Toyota Corolla
Cross in the year-to-date top ten list

79
00:03:53,330 --> 00:03:54,320
none of them made it.

80
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:55,160
The reason is value.

81
00:03:55,210 --> 00:04:01,100
Right now, the Jolion Premium
Hybrid is $32,990 drive-away,

82
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:05,380
with GWM adding a three-thousand-dollar
deposit contribution until the end of

83
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:06,280
November.

84
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:08,680
That's a lot of small
SUV, with a hybrid engine,

85
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:11,140
for the price of a basic petrol rival.

86
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:13,240
And the Jolion shows something important:

87
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:15,600
not every Chinese success is electric.

88
00:04:15,650 --> 00:04:17,160
Plenty of Australians want a cheap,

89
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:20,800
efficient hybrid that works just like
their old petrol car and the Jolion

90
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:22,520
gives them exactly that.

91
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:26,930
GWM as a brand has had a tougher few
months, but the Jolion has been its rock.

92
00:04:28,453 --> 00:04:29,970
Number eight: the Toyota Prado.

93
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,490
Here's a comeback story.

94
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:34,530
In early 2026, Prado sales fell hard.

95
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,750
Toyota said that was mainly
about supply, not demand.

96
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:41,530
In the first five months of the year,
Prado sales were down 45 per cent.

97
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:44,550
Then the supply came back
and so did the buyers.

98
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,210
In October 2026,

99
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:48,970
the Prado was the sixth
best-selling vehicle in Australia,

100
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:54,850
with 2,397 sales, up 64 per cent
on the same month last year.

101
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,950
By the end of October,

102
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,610
the Prado had moved ahead of
the Ford Everest for the year,

103
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:04,770
with 18,062 sales against
the Everest's 17,944.

104
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:08,130
That matters, because the Everest
has been the Prado's biggest rival,

105
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,970
and for a while it looked like
Ford was winning that fight.

106
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,610
The new Prado is bigger,

107
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:14,590
tougher and more modern than the old one,

108
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:18,050
and Australians clearly still want a
proper LandCruiser-badged four-by-four

109
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,510
for towing and touring.

110
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,050
It's proof that even in the
middle of the Chinese boom,

111
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:25,220
a strong nameplate with the
right product can still win.

112
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:29,104
Number seven: the Chery Tiggo 4.

113
00:05:29,154 --> 00:05:32,244
Two years ago, most Australians
had never heard of Chery.

114
00:05:32,294 --> 00:05:37,104
In 2026, its little Tiggo 4 is one of
the most popular cars in the country.

115
00:05:37,154 --> 00:05:38,924
In the first nine months of the year,

116
00:05:38,974 --> 00:05:43,874
the Tiggo 4 sold 19,865
cars, up 43 per cent.

117
00:05:43,924 --> 00:05:47,224
That's sixth in the whole country
and ahead of the Hyundai Kona,

118
00:05:47,274 --> 00:05:50,044
which sold 18,533.

119
00:05:50,094 --> 00:05:51,524
In the first half of the year,

120
00:05:51,574 --> 00:05:54,124
it was ahead of both the
Kona and the Haval Jolion.

121
00:05:54,174 --> 00:05:55,044
The reason is price.

122
00:05:55,094 --> 00:06:01,084
Right now, the Tiggo 4
Urban is $23,990 drive-away,

123
00:06:01,134 --> 00:06:05,864
with a $1,500 fuel card, according
to the deals tracker CarSorted.

124
00:06:05,914 --> 00:06:09,624
That's thousands of dollars less than
most of the small SUVs it's beating.

125
00:06:09,674 --> 00:06:11,504
And Chery as a brand is flying.

126
00:06:11,554 --> 00:06:13,014
In the first half of 2026,

127
00:06:13,064 --> 00:06:17,644
Chery's sales were up 77 per cent,
and almost every model it sells grew.

128
00:06:17,694 --> 00:06:22,044
In October, the Tiggo 4 was again
inside the national top ten,

129
00:06:22,094 --> 00:06:24,654
with 2,178 sales.

130
00:06:25,554 --> 00:06:27,754
Number six: the Jaecoo J5.

131
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:30,924
Jaecoo is a sister brand
to Chery and Omoda,

132
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:34,184
and it's barely been in Australia long
enough for most people to learn how to

133
00:06:34,234 --> 00:06:34,984
say it.

134
00:06:35,034 --> 00:06:38,484
But its J5 small SUV has
gone off like a rocket.

135
00:06:38,534 --> 00:06:40,404
According to ACM's motoring team,

136
00:06:40,454 --> 00:06:45,224
the J5 sold more than eleven thousand
cars in the first nine months of 2026.

137
00:06:45,274 --> 00:06:50,344
And the Omoda Jaecoo group was up 621
per cent for the year to September.

138
00:06:50,394 --> 00:06:51,044
Why?

139
00:06:51,094 --> 00:06:52,084
Price and style.

140
00:06:52,134 --> 00:06:57,004
The J5 petrol launched
at $25,990 drive-away,

141
00:06:57,054 --> 00:07:02,764
and the electric J5 EV was
priced at $36,990 drive-away.

142
00:07:02,814 --> 00:07:03,644
It has a boxy,

143
00:07:03,694 --> 00:07:07,164
upmarket look that some people say
reminds them of a much more expensive

144
00:07:07,214 --> 00:07:08,904
European SUV.

145
00:07:08,954 --> 00:07:12,684
The J5 EV had more than four thousand
orders within months of launch,

146
00:07:12,734 --> 00:07:13,844
according to The Beep.

147
00:07:13,894 --> 00:07:17,304
The J5 shows how fast a new
brand can grow in Australia now.

148
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:21,444
A few years ago, a new brand would have
taken a decade to build a following.

149
00:07:21,494 --> 00:07:23,434
Jaecoo did it in about a year.

150
00:07:24,952 --> 00:07:26,294
Number five: the Zeekr 7X.

151
00:07:26,344 --> 00:07:29,384
Zeekr is Geely's premium electric brand.

152
00:07:29,434 --> 00:07:31,724
It's competing against Tesla, BMW,

153
00:07:31,774 --> 00:07:35,564
Mercedes and Audi and in 2026,
it's beating a lot of them.

154
00:07:35,614 --> 00:07:37,244
In the first nine months of the year,

155
00:07:37,294 --> 00:07:43,344
Zeekr's sales were up 1,560
per cent to 12,120 cars.

156
00:07:43,394 --> 00:07:49,444
In October alone, Zeekr sold
1,874 cars, up 767 per cent.

157
00:07:49,494 --> 00:07:54,184
And the star is the Zeekr
7X, a mid-size electric SUV.

158
00:07:54,234 --> 00:07:57,744
The Driven reported in May that it had
become Australia's best-selling premium

159
00:07:57,794 --> 00:08:01,924
SUV, and in July it cracked the
national top ten for the first time.

160
00:08:01,974 --> 00:08:03,904
Think about how remarkable that is.

161
00:08:03,954 --> 00:08:05,304
A premium electric SUV,

162
00:08:05,354 --> 00:08:08,244
from a brand that only
launched in Australia recently,

163
00:08:08,294 --> 00:08:10,684
outselling famous European luxury names.

164
00:08:10,734 --> 00:08:13,484
The 7X wins on technology and value:

165
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:16,104
long range, fast charging,
a luxurious cabin,

166
00:08:16,154 --> 00:08:19,284
and a price that undercuts
many European rivals.

167
00:08:19,334 --> 00:08:22,644
And while the brands that were here first
have been cutting prices to keep up,

168
00:08:22,694 --> 00:08:24,544
Zeekr has been taking orders.

169
00:08:24,594 --> 00:08:27,844
If you want to know where the luxury
car market in Australia is heading,

170
00:08:27,894 --> 00:08:28,854
look at this car.

171
00:08:29,589 --> 00:08:32,359
Number four: the Toyota HiLux.

172
00:08:32,409 --> 00:08:34,559
Australia's favourite ute is back on top.

173
00:08:34,609 --> 00:08:36,219
In October 2026,

174
00:08:36,269 --> 00:08:38,779
the HiLux was the best-selling
vehicle in the whole country,

175
00:08:38,829 --> 00:08:44,659
with 5,954 sales, up 34 per cent
on the same month last year.

176
00:08:44,709 --> 00:08:47,599
It beat the Ford Ranger by
more than a thousand units.

177
00:08:47,649 --> 00:08:50,359
That's a big deal, because
it had been a tough year.

178
00:08:50,409 --> 00:08:52,739
The Ranger led the
market for most of 2026,

179
00:08:52,789 --> 00:08:56,819
and in the first nine months, HiLux
sales were down about ten per cent.

180
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:59,379
The new-generation HiLux
arrived during the year,

181
00:08:59,429 --> 00:09:00,839
and buyers were waiting for it.

182
00:09:00,889 --> 00:09:03,359
And Toyota is fighting harder than usual.

183
00:09:03,409 --> 00:09:07,919
It's offering a four-thousand-dollar
finance deposit bonus on the HiLux SR5 a

184
00:09:07,969 --> 00:09:09,399
rare move for Toyota.

185
00:09:09,449 --> 00:09:12,179
The new range also includes
an electric version.

186
00:09:12,229 --> 00:09:14,679
Now, the HiLux isn't growing
the way the Chinese brands are.

187
00:09:14,729 --> 00:09:17,699
But it shows that the old
champions aren't finished.

188
00:09:17,749 --> 00:09:20,639
When Toyota gets the product
and the supply right,

189
00:09:20,689 --> 00:09:21,899
Australians still line up for it.

190
00:09:21,949 --> 00:09:25,599
And the battle between the HiLux and
the Ranger for the number one spot in

191
00:09:25,649 --> 00:09:28,449
2026 is going right down to the wire.

192
00:09:29,227 --> 00:09:31,517
Number three: the Geely EX5.

193
00:09:31,567 --> 00:09:34,057
This is the car from
the start of the video.

194
00:09:34,107 --> 00:09:36,037
In September 2026,

195
00:09:36,087 --> 00:09:40,457
Geely EX5 sales were up 620 per
cent on September last year.

196
00:09:40,507 --> 00:09:44,877
In July, it was up 315 per cent
and ninth in the national rankings.

197
00:09:44,927 --> 00:09:45,777
And in October,

198
00:09:45,827 --> 00:09:47,957
it was the tenth best-selling
vehicle in the country,

199
00:09:48,007 --> 00:09:52,857
with 1,789 sales, up
more than 420 per cent.

200
00:09:52,907 --> 00:09:58,257
Geely as a brand sold 23,632 cars in
the first nine months of the year,

201
00:09:58,307 --> 00:10:00,217
up 639 per cent.

202
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:05,677
In October alone, it sold
4,365, up 520 per cent.

203
00:10:05,727 --> 00:10:10,267
In May, GoAuto reported that Geely had
passed ten thousand sales in Australia.

204
00:10:10,317 --> 00:10:13,197
The EX5 is a mid-size electric SUV,

205
00:10:13,247 --> 00:10:17,797
priced at $41,990 before on-road costs,

206
00:10:17,847 --> 00:10:21,277
and right now Geely is offering
novated lease discounts on top.

207
00:10:21,327 --> 00:10:24,877
That makes it one of the cheapest
mid-size electric SUVs you can buy.

208
00:10:24,927 --> 00:10:26,577
Geely isn't a small company, either.

209
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:28,657
It owns Volvo and Zeekr,

210
00:10:28,707 --> 00:10:30,577
it controls Polestar and Lotus,

211
00:10:30,627 --> 00:10:34,117
and its founder is one of the biggest
shareholders in Mercedes-Benz.

212
00:10:34,167 --> 00:10:38,237
So the EX5 isn't a cheap gamble from an
unknown brand it's one of the biggest

213
00:10:38,287 --> 00:10:41,587
car groups in the world finally
getting serious about Australia.

214
00:10:43,237 --> 00:10:45,545
Number two: the BYD Sealion 7.

215
00:10:45,595 --> 00:10:48,845
The Sealion 7 is a mid-size electric SUV,

216
00:10:48,895 --> 00:10:51,705
and it's become one of the most
important cars in Australia.

217
00:10:51,755 --> 00:10:54,085
In the first nine months of 2026,

218
00:10:54,135 --> 00:10:58,865
it sold 19,964 cars, up 135 per cent,

219
00:10:58,915 --> 00:11:03,005
and finished fifth in the whole
country above the Isuzu D-Max,

220
00:11:03,055 --> 00:11:05,145
the Hyundai Kona and the Ford Everest.

221
00:11:05,195 --> 00:11:06,535
In the first half of the year,

222
00:11:06,585 --> 00:11:12,945
it was BYD's best-selling model,
with 12,516 sales, up 233 per cent.

223
00:11:12,995 --> 00:11:18,105
And in October, it was fifth
again, with 2,524 sales.

224
00:11:18,155 --> 00:11:22,705
The Sealion 7 gives buyers a big electric
SUV with a lot of technology at a

225
00:11:22,755 --> 00:11:25,585
price that undercuts many
rivals and right now,

226
00:11:25,635 --> 00:11:28,185
BYD is adding four
thousand dollars cashback,

227
00:11:28,235 --> 00:11:33,685
bringing the Sealion 7 Premium
to $50,990 before on-road costs.

228
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:37,805
And it carried BYD to a place no
Chinese brand had been before.

229
00:11:37,855 --> 00:11:41,725
BYD finished second in the national
brand rankings every month from April to

230
00:11:41,775 --> 00:11:42,605
October.

231
00:11:42,655 --> 00:11:47,785
In October, it sold 10,025
cars, up 153 per cent.

232
00:11:47,835 --> 00:11:50,855
The Sealion 7 is the car
that made that possible.

233
00:11:51,694 --> 00:11:53,884
And number one: the Tesla Model Y.

234
00:11:53,934 --> 00:11:56,484
In the first nine months of 2026,

235
00:11:56,534 --> 00:12:01,064
